    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
    "caseLabel": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "new-mixed-25",
    "sourceId": "mixed:25",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You have a Fabric tenant that contains a lakehouse.</p><p>You plan to use a Fabric notebook and PySpark to read sales data and save the data as a Delta table named Sales.</p><p>The table must be partitioned by Sales Year and Quarter.</p><p>You load the sales data to a DataFrame named df that contains a Year column and a Quarter column.</p><p>Which command should you run next?</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "df.write.mode(\"overwrite\").format(\"delta\").partitionBy(\"Year\",Quarter\").save(\"Files/Sales)"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "df.write.mode(\"overwrite\").format(\"delta\").partitionBy(\"Year\",\"Quarter\").save(\"Tables/Sales\")"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "df.write.mode(\"overwrite\").format(\"parquet\").partitionBy(\"Year\",\"Quarter\").save(\"Files/Sales\")"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "df.write.mode(\"overwrite\").format(\"parquet\").partitionBy(\"Year\",\"Quarter\").save(\"Tables/Sales)"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>Managed Delta tables are written to the Tables folder in Delta format, partitioned by the Year and Quarter columns. The Files folder holds raw files, not tables, and parquet is not the Delta format.</p>Key verified against the documentation.",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "mixed:25"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
    "caseLabel": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "new-mixed-26",
    "sourceId": "mixed:26",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You have a Fabric workspace that contains a complex semantic model for a Microsoft Power BI report.</p><p>You need to optimize the semantic model for analytical queries and use denormalization to reduce the model complexity and the number of joins between tables.</p><p>Which tables should you denormalize?</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "dimension tables on the same level of granularity"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "fact tables on the same level of granularity"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "role-playing dimension tables"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "Snowflake dimension tables"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>Denormalizing snowflake dimension tables — flattening the normalized dimension hierarchies into single wide dimensions — removes joins between the dimension tables and simplifies the model into a star schema.</p>Key verified against the documentation.",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "mixed:26"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
    "caseLabel": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "new-mixed-27",
    "sourceId": "mixed:27",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>Which of the following is a key benefit of using Microsoft Fabric in data projects?</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "It allows data professionals to work on data projects independently, without the need for collaboration."
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "It requires duplication of data across different systems and teams to ensure data availability."
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "It provides a single, integrated environment for data professionals and the business to collaborate on data projects."
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>Fabric is a single, integrated analytics platform: one copy of the data in OneLake, shared across the lakehouse, warehouse, dataflows, notebooks and Power BI, so data professionals and the business collaborate on the same data instead of duplicating it across systems.</p>Key verified against the documentation.",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "mixed:27"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
    "caseLabel": ""
  },
  {
