    "caseLabel": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "new-mixed-35",
    "sourceId": "mixed:35",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You have a managed table based on a folder that contains data files in delta format. If you drop the table, what happens?</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "The table metadata and data files are deleted."
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "The table definition is removed from the metastore, but the data files remain intact."
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "The table definition remains in the metastore, but the data files are deleted."
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>For a managed table, Spark owns both the metadata and the data, so dropping the table deletes the metadata from the metastore and the underlying data files. For an external table, only the metadata would be removed.</p>Key verified against the documentation.",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "mixed:35"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
    "caseLabel": ""
  },
