  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q53",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q53",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You have a Fabric tenant that contains a lakehouse named Lakehouse1. Lakehouse1 contains a table named Nyctaxi_raw. Nyctaxi_row contains\nthe following table:\nYou create a Fabric notebook and attach it to Lakehouse1.\nYou need to use PySpark code to transform the data. The solution must meet the following requirements:\nAdd a column named pickupDate that will contain only the date portion of pickupDateTime.\nFilter the DataFrame to include only rows where fareAmount is a positive number that is less than 100.\nHow should you complete the code? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "0",
        "label": "df2 =  ______  ('pickupDate', df['tpepPickupDateTime']",
        "options": [
          "df.columns",
          "df.select",
          "df.withColumn",
          "df.withColumnsRenamed"
        ],
        "answer": "df.withColumn"
      },
      {
        "id": "1",
        "label": "______  \\   (applied to the column expression)",
        "options": [
          ".alias('date')",
          ".cast('date')",
          ".cast('pickupDate')",
          ".getfield('date')"
        ],
        "answer": ".cast('date')"
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "label": "______   (the filter step)",
        "options": [
          ".filter(\"fareAmount > 0 AND fareAmount < 100\")",
          ".filter(col(\"fareAmount\").contains(\"1..100\"))",
          ".when(df.fareAmount > 0 AND fareAmount < 100)",
          ".where(df.fareAmount.isin([1,100]))"
        ],
        "answer": ".filter(\"fareAmount > 0 AND fareAmount < 100\")"
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>The completed code:\n\n```python\ndf = spark.read.format(&quot;delta&quot;).load(&quot;Tables/nyctaxi_raw&quot;)\ndf2 = df.withColumn(&quot;pickupDate&quot;, df[&#x27;tpepPickupDateTime&#x27;].cast(&#x27;date&#x27;)) \\\n        .filter(&quot;fareAmount &gt; 0 AND fareAmount &lt; 100&quot;)\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — `df.withColumn`.** The requirement is to **add** a column named `pickupDate`. `withColumn(colName, col)` *&quot;returns a new DataFrame by adding a column or replacing the existing column that has the same name&quot;* — and its two-argument shape matches the code.\n- `df.select` projects columns; it would drop everything not listed.\n- `df.withColumnsRenamed` **renames** existing columns (and takes a dict), which loses `tpepPickupDateTime`.\n- `df.columns` is a property returning a list of names, not a function.\n\n**Blank 2 — `.cast(&#x27;date&#x27;)`.** Only the **date portion** is wanted, so the timestamp is cast to Spark&#x27;s `DateType`, which truncates the time. `.cast(&#x27;pickupDate&#x27;)` is not a type. `.alias(&#x27;date&#x27;)` only labels the column — it would leave the full timestamp value, and the name is already set by `withColumn`. `.getfield(&#x27;date&#x27;)` reads a subfield of a struct.\n\n**Blank 3 — `.filter(&quot;fareAmount &gt; 0 AND fareAmount &lt; 100&quot;)`.** `filter` accepts a SQL expression string, and this one states exactly &quot;positive and less than 100&quot;.\n- `.contains(&quot;1..100&quot;)` is substring matching on text — wrong on every count.\n- `.when(...)` is a **column** function used inside `select`/`withColumn`; it is not a DataFrame method and cannot filter rows.\n- `.isin([1,100])` matches the two literal values 1 and 100, not the range between them.</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "PySpark basics",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/databricks/pyspark/basics?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938#transform-data-with-dataframes"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [
      "Original question exhibit files not supplied: p149_i1.png, p149_i2.png"
