    "id": "new-json-t1q54",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q54",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a unique solution that\nmight meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others might not have a correct solution.\nAfter you answer a question in this section, you will NOT be able to return to it. As a result, these questions will not appear in the review screen.\nYou have a Fabric tenant that contains a new semantic model in OneLake.\nYou use a Fabric notebook to read the data into a Spark DataFrame.\nYou need to evaluate the data to calculate the min, max, mean, and standard deviation values for all the string and numeric columns.\nSolution: You use the following PySpark expression:\ndf.explain()\nDoes this meet the goal?</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "Yes"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "No"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>**No.** `df.explain()` prints the **query plan** — the parsed, analyzed, optimized logical plans and the physical plan Spark intends to run. It is a debugging and tuning tool. It computes no statistics at all, so it returns no min, max, mean or standard deviation.\n\nThe solution that meets the goal is **`df.summary()`** (see T1Q56), which returns count, mean, stddev, min, the quartiles and max, and covers string columns as well as numeric ones. `df.describe()` is the narrower sibling.\n\nAcross this set of four:\n\n| Question | Expression | Meets the goal? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **T1Q54** | `df.explain()` | **No** — prints the query plan |\n| T1Q55 | `df.show()` | No — prints the first 20 rows |\n| **T1Q56** | `df.summary()` | **Yes** |\n| — | `df.describe()` | Yes (the other documented answer) |</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "explain",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/databricks/pyspark/reference/classes/dataframe/explain?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "json:T1Q54"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "missingExhibits": [],
    "missingAnswerImages": []
