  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q92",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q92",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You have a custom Direct Lake semantic model named Model1 that has one billion rows of data.\nYou use Tabular Editor to connect to Model1 by using the XMLA endpoint.\nYou need to ensure that when users interact with reports based on Model1, their queries always use Direct Lake mode.\nWhat should you do?</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "From Model, configure the Default Mode option."
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "From Partitions, configure the Mode option."
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "From Model, configure the Storage Location option."
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "From Model, configure the Direct Lake Behavior option."
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>A Direct Lake model can silently **fall back to DirectQuery** when data cannot be loaded efficiently into memory (guardrail exceeded, a view rather than a table, RLS on the warehouse, and so on). The switch that governs this is the model-level **`DirectLakeBehavior`** property, exposed in Tabular Editor as **Direct Lake Behavior** on the Model node:\n\n| Value | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Automatic` (default) | Direct Lake, falling back to DirectQuery when needed |\n| **`DirectLakeOnly`** | **Direct Lake only — a query that cannot use it fails instead of falling back** |\n| `DirectQueryOnly` | always DirectQuery |\n\nTo guarantee that *&quot;their queries always use Direct Lake mode&quot;*, set it to **Direct Lake only**.\n\n- **B Partitions → Mode** – a Direct Lake table has a single `DirectLake` partition; this does not control fallback.\n- **A Model → Default Mode** – sets the storage mode for *new* tables, not the fallback policy.\n- **C Model → Storage Location** – where the model data sits. Unrelated.</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "Direct Lake overview — fallback behavior",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/fabric/fundamentals/direct-lake-overview?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "json:T1Q92"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "missingExhibits": [],
    "missingAnswerImages": []
  },
  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q93",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q93",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You create a semantic model by using Microsoft Power BI Desktop. The model contains one security role named SalesRegionManager and the\nfollowing tables:\n• Sales\n• SalesRegion\n• SalesAddress\nYou need to modify the model to ensure that users assigned the SalesRegionManager role cannot see a column named Address in SalesAddress.\nWhich three actions should you perform in sequence? To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and\narrange them in the correct order.</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "0",
        "label": "Step 1",
        "options": [
          "Open the model in Power BI Desktop.",
          "Open the model in Tabular Editor.",
          "Select the Address column in SalesAddress.",
          "Set the Hidden property to True.",
          "Set Object Level Security to Default for SalesRegionManager.",
          "Set Object Level Security to None for SalesRegionManager."
        ],
        "answer": "Open the model in Tabular Editor."
      },
      {
        "id": "1",
        "label": "Step 2",
        "options": [
          "Open the model in Power BI Desktop.",
          "Open the model in Tabular Editor.",
          "Select the Address column in SalesAddress.",
          "Set the Hidden property to True.",
          "Set Object Level Security to Default for SalesRegionManager.",
          "Set Object Level Security to None for SalesRegionManager."
        ],
        "answer": "Select the Address column in SalesAddress."
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "label": "Step 3",
        "options": [
          "Open the model in Power BI Desktop.",
          "Open the model in Tabular Editor.",
          "Select the Address column in SalesAddress.",
          "Set the Hidden property to True.",
          "Set Object Level Security to Default for SalesRegionManager.",
          "Set Object Level Security to None for SalesRegionManager."
        ],
        "answer": "Set Object Level Security to None for SalesRegionManager."
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>Hiding a column *from a specific role* is **object-level security (OLS)**, and OLS is per-role metadata you cannot author in Power BI Desktop.\n\n1. **Open the model in Tabular Editor.** The doc: *&quot;To create roles on Power BI Desktop semantic models, use external tools such as Tabular Editor.&quot;* Desktop can create RLS roles and DAX filters, but not OLS.\n2. **Select the Address column in SalesAddress.** OLS is set on the object being secured, under the role&#x27;s *Table Permissions*.\n3. **Set Object Level Security to `None` for SalesRegionManager.** The two values are documented as:\n\n| OLS value | Effect for that role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Read` | the table or column is **visible** |\n| **`None`** | **OLS is enforced — the table or column is hidden from that role**; to its members it is as if the object does not exist |\n\nRejected steps:\n- **Set the Hidden property to True** – hides the column from the field list **for everyone**, in every role, and it is only cosmetic: the column is still queryable. It secures nothing.\n- **Set OLS to `Default`** – inherits, which leaves the column visible.\n- **Open the model in Power BI Desktop** – cannot set OLS.</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "Object-level security in Microsoft Fabric",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/fabric/security/service-admin-object-level-security?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [
      "Original question exhibit files not supplied: p244_i1.png"
    ],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "json:T1Q93"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "missingExhibits": [
      "p244_i1.png"
    ],
    "missingAnswerImages": [
