  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q101",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q101",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You have a Fabric tenant that contains customer churn data stored as Parquet files in OneLake. The data contains details about customer\ndemographics and product usage.\nYou create a Fabric notebook to read the data into a Spark DataFrame. You then create column charts in the notebook that show the distribution\nof retained customers as compared to lost customers based on geography, the number of products purchased, age, and customer tenure.\nWhich type of analytics are you performing?</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "diagnostic"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "descriptive"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "prescriptive"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "predictive"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "B"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>**Descriptive.** The work described is: read the data, then draw column charts showing the **distribution** of retained versus lost customers across geography, products purchased, age and tenure. That is summarising and presenting **what happened** — the definition of descriptive analytics.\n\n- **A diagnostic** – the trap, at 22% of the vote, because slicing by four attributes *feels* like investigating causes. But diagnostic analytics establishes **why**: drill-down into root cause, correlation analysis, hypothesis testing. Charting distributions does not attribute causation — it shows the shape of the data and leaves the *why* to the reader.\n- **D predictive** would score each customer with a churn probability (a trained model).\n- **C prescriptive** would recommend the retention action to take.\n\n*(Compare T1Q98, the same taxonomy tested with a simpler exhibit.)*</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "Data analysis and analytics types",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/get-started-data-analytics/?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "json:T1Q101"
    ],
