  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q102",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q102",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You have a Fabric tenant that contains a semantic model. The model contains data about retail stores.\nYou need to write a DAX query that will be executed by using the XMLA endpoint. The query must return the total amount of sales from the same\nperiod last year.\nHow should you complete the DAX expression? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "0",
        "label": "VAR _LYSales =  ______  ( [Total Sales], SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR ( 'Orders'[Order Date] ) )",
        "options": [
          "CALCULATE",
          "CALCULATETABLE",
          "FILTER",
          "SUMMARIZE",
          "SUMMARIZECOLUMNS"
        ],
        "answer": "CALCULATE"
      },
      {
        "id": "1",
        "label": "RETURN  ______",
        "options": [
          "[Total Sales]",
          "_LYSales",
          "{ _LYSales }",
          "VAR"
        ],
        "answer": "{ _LYSales }"
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>**CALCULATE — `{ _LYSales }`.**\n\n```dax\nEVALUATE\nVAR _LYSales =\n    CALCULATE ( [Total Sales], SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR ( &#x27;Orders&#x27;[Order Date] ) )\nRETURN\n    { _LYSales }\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — `CALCULATE`.** `[Total Sales]` is a **scalar** measure and `SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR(...)` is a filter to apply to it. `CALCULATE(&lt;scalar expression&gt;, &lt;filter&gt;…)` is the function for that shape.\n- `CALCULATETABLE` has the same semantics but takes and returns a **table**; `[Total Sales]` is not a table.\n- `FILTER`, `SUMMARIZE` and `SUMMARIZECOLUMNS` all return tables and do not take a measure as a first argument. (A commenter with +58 notes the printed distractor `SUMMARIZE` is a common wrong pick.)\n\n**Blank 2 — `{ _LYSales }`, and here the PDF answer key is wrong** (it marks the bare `_LYSales`).\n\n`EVALUATE` is documented as taking a **table expression**: *&quot;EVALUATE ( &lt;Table&gt; ) … The table expression to be evaluated and returned.&quot;* `_LYSales` holds a **scalar** — the output of `CALCULATE` over a measure — so `RETURN _LYSales` does not type-check. Run it and the engine rejects the query: *&quot;The expression specified in the query is not a valid table expression.&quot;*\n\nThe braces are DAX&#x27;s **table constructor**. `{ _LYSales }` wraps the scalar into a one-row, one-column table (`[Value]`), which is a valid `EVALUATE` operand and returns the number you want.\n\n| RETURN | Type | Valid after EVALUATE? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `[Total Sales]` | scalar — and the *current-year* figure, not last year&#x27;s | no |\n| `_LYSales` | scalar | **no** |\n| **`{ _LYSales }`** | **table (1×1)** | **yes** |\n| `VAR` | a keyword, not an expression | no |\n\n*Note:* the community comment that addresses this blank (+12) makes the same point. The two higher-voted comments only discuss blank 1.</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "EVALUATE statement (DAX)",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/dax/evaluate-statement-dax?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      },
      {
        "title": "Table constructor in DAX",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/dax/table-constructor?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      },
      {
        "title": "SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR function (DAX)",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/dax/sameperiodlastyear-function-dax?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [
      "Original question exhibit files not supplied: p263_i1.png"
    ],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "json:T1Q102"
