  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q104",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q104",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You have a Fabric tenant that contains a Microsoft Power BI report.\nYou are exploring a new semantic model.\nYou need to display the following column statistics:\n• Count\n• Average\n• Null count\n• Distinct count\n• Standard deviation\nWhich Power Query function should you run?</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "Table.schema"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "Table.view"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "Table.FuzzyGroup"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "Table.Profile"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>**`Table.Profile`** returns one row per column with exactly the statistics listed. The doc enumerates them: *&quot;minimum, maximum, average, standard deviation, count, null count, distinct count.&quot;* All five requested values — Count, Average, Null count, Distinct count and Standard deviation — are in that set.\n\n- **A `Table.Schema`** – returns *metadata*: column names, positions, data types, nullability. No statistics. (It is also spelled with a capital S.)\n- **B `Table.View`** – an advanced function for building a custom query folding handler. Nothing to do with profiling.\n- **C `Table.FuzzyGroup`** – groups rows by approximate similarity of a key.\n\n*(Same function as T1Q14, asked from the statistics side rather than the maximum-value side.)*</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "Table.Profile — Power Query M",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/powerquery-m/table-profile?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "json:T1Q104"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "missingExhibits": [],
    "missingAnswerImages": []
