  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q140",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q140",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You have a Microsoft Power Bl project that contains a file named definition.pbir. definition.pbir contains the following JSON.\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "0",
        "label": "definition.pbir is in the PBIR-Legacy format.",
        "options": [
          "Yes",
          "No"
        ],
        "answer": "Yes"
      },
      {
        "id": "1",
        "label": "The semantic model referenced by definition.pbir is located in the Power BI service.",
        "options": [
          "Yes",
          "No"
        ],
        "answer": "No"
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "label": "When the related report is opened, Power BI Desktop will open the semantic model in full edit mode.",
        "options": [
          "Yes",
          "No"
        ],
        "answer": "Yes"
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>**Yes — No — Yes.** The file is\n\n```json\n{\n  &quot;version&quot;: &quot;1.0&quot;,\n  &quot;datasetReference&quot;: {\n    &quot;byPath&quot;: { &quot;path&quot;: &quot;../Sales.Dataset&quot; },\n    &quot;byConnection&quot;: null\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**1. PBIR-Legacy → Yes.** *(The PDF answer-key image marks **No**; it is wrong.)* The `version` property is precisely what declares the report definition format, and the doc gives the mapping as a table:\n\n| Version | Supported formats |\n| --- | --- |\n| **1.0** | **Report definition must be stored as PBIR-Legacy in the `report.json` file.** |\n| 4.0 or higher | Report definition can be stored as PBIR-Legacy (`report.json`) **or** PBIR (`\\definition` folder). |\n\nAt `&quot;version&quot;: &quot;1.0&quot;` the report definition *must* be PBIR-Legacy — there is no other option at that version. (Microsoft&#x27;s own example of the current format uses `&quot;version&quot;: &quot;4.0&quot;`.) The highest-voted comment asserts that *&quot;1.0 isn&#x27;t legacy format … the version would be blank if it was legacy&quot;*, which the documented table contradicts; a later comment answers Yes.\n\n**2. The model is in the Power BI service → No.** The reference is **`byPath`**, a *relative path to a local folder* (`../Sales.Dataset`), and `byConnection` is explicitly `null`. `byConnection` is the one that *&quot;specifies the connection to a semantic model in a Fabric workspace by using a connection string&quot;* — it is not in use here.\n\n**3. Desktop opens the model in full edit mode → Yes.** Straight from the doc, on `byPath`: *&quot;When used, Power BI Desktop **also opens the semantic model in full edit mode**.&quot;* The contrast is stated in the next line: *&quot;When a `byConnection` reference is used, Power BI Desktop doesn&#x27;t open the semantic model in edit mode.&quot;*</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "Power BI Desktop project report folder — definition.pbir",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/developer/projects/projects-report?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [
      "Original question exhibit files not supplied: p338_i1.png, p338_i2.png"
    ],
