  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q156",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q156",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You have a Fabric tenant that contains the workspaces shown in the following table.\nYou have a deployment pipeline named Pipeline1 that deploys items from Workspace_DEV to Workspace_TEST. In Pipeline1, all items that have\nmatching names are paired.\nYou deploy the contents of Workspace_DEV to Workspace_TEST by using Pipeline1.\nWhat will the contents of Workspace_TEST be once the deployment is complete?</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "Lakehouse1 - Lakehouse2 - Notebook1 - Notebook2 - Pipeline1 - SemanticModel1"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "Lakehouse1 - Notebook1 - Pipeline1 - SemanticModel1"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "Lakehouse2 - Notebook2 - SemanticModel1"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "Lakehouse2 - Notebook2 - Pipeline1 - SemanticModel1"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>Deployment **adds and overwrites; it never deletes**. The doc: *&quot;the items being copied from the source stage overwrite the paired item in the stage you&#x27;re in according to the pairing rules. **Items that don&#x27;t exist in the source stage remain as is.**&quot;*\n\nWork it through. Only items with **matching names** are paired:\n\n| Workspace_DEV | Workspace_TEST (before) | Paired? | Workspace_TEST (after) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Lakehouse1 | — | no | **Lakehouse1** (new) |\n| — | Lakehouse2 | no | Lakehouse2 (untouched) |\n| Notebook1 | — | no | **Notebook1** (new) |\n| — | Notebook2 | no | Notebook2 (untouched) |\n| Pipeline1 | — | no | **Pipeline1** (new) |\n| SemanticModel1 | SemanticModel1 | **yes** | SemanticModel1 (overwritten) |\n\nThe result is the **union**: Lakehouse1, Lakehouse2, Notebook1, Notebook2, Pipeline1, SemanticModel1 — **A**.\n\n- **B** is Workspace_DEV&#x27;s contents, as if deployment replaced the whole workspace. It does not.\n- **C / D** drop the newly deployed items.\n\n*(Note &quot;Pipeline1&quot; here is a **data pipeline item** in Workspace_DEV, distinct from the deployment pipeline doing the deploying — a confusing naming choice in the question, and one commenter is caught by it.)*</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "Overview of Fabric deployment pipelines — item pairing",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/fabric/cicd/deployment-pipelines/intro-to-deployment-pipelines?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [
      "Original question exhibit files not supplied: p366_i1.png"
    ],
