  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q157",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q157",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Workspace_DEV. Workspace_DEV contains the semantic models shown in the\nfollowing table.\nWorkspace_DEV contains the dataflows shown in the following table.\nYou create a new workspace named Workspace_TEST.\nYou create a deployment pipeline named Pipeline1 to move items from Workspace_DEV to Workspace_TEST.\nYou run Pipeline1.\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "0",
        "label": "DF1 will be deployed to Workspace_TEST.",
        "options": [
          "Yes",
          "No"
        ],
        "answer": "Yes"
      },
      {
        "id": "1",
        "label": "Data from Model1 will be deployed to Workspace_TEST.",
        "options": [
          "Yes",
          "No"
        ],
        "answer": "No"
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "label": "The scheduled refresh policy for Model1 will be deployed to Workspace_TEST.",
        "options": [
          "Yes",
          "No"
        ],
        "answer": "No"
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>**Yes — No — No. The PDF answer-key image (No / Yes / Yes) is wrong on all three**, and the documentation settles each one outright.\n\n**1. DF1 (a Dataflow **Gen1**) will be deployed → Yes.** The supported-items list carries two separate entries: **&quot;Dataflows gen2&quot;** under *Data Factory items*, and plain **&quot;Dataflow *(preview)*&quot;** under *Power BI items* — the latter is Gen1. The dataflow-limitations section confirms Gen1 goes through the pipeline by noting a Gen1-specific caveat: *&quot;Incremental refresh settings aren&#x27;t copied in Gen 1.&quot;* You would not document a copy limitation for an item type that is never deployed.\n\n**2. Data from Model1 will be deployed → No.** From *Item properties that are not copied*: *&quot;**Data — Data isn&#x27;t copied. Only metadata is copied**.&quot;* The same point is made when assigning a workspace: *&quot;the semantic model refresh is required because **data isn&#x27;t copied from one stage to another**.&quot;*\n\n**3. The scheduled refresh policy for Model1 will be deployed → No.** The doc lists the semantic model properties that are **not** copied:\n\n&gt; - Role assignment\n&gt; - **Refresh schedule**\n&gt; - Data source credentials\n&gt; - Query caching settings\n&gt; - Endorsement settings\n\n*(Do not confuse this with the **incremental refresh policy**, which *is* copied: *&quot;When you deploy the semantic model, the policy is copied along.&quot;* A refresh **schedule** and an incremental-refresh **policy** are different things.)*\n\n*Community:* the top comment (+21) gives Yes/No/No, and another (+5) reports testing it — *&quot;I tested and refresh schedule is not deployed: Y,N,N&quot;*. A third (+11) says No/No/No on the belief that Gen1 dataflows are unsupported, which the supported-items list contradicts.</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "The Fabric deployment pipelines process — properties copied and not copied",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/fabric/cicd/deployment-pipelines/understand-the-deployment-process?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      },
      {
        "title": "Overview of Fabric deployment pipelines — supported items",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/fabric/cicd/deployment-pipelines/intro-to-deployment-pipelines?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [
      "Original question exhibit files not supplied: p368_i1.png, p368_i2.png, p368_i3.png"
    ],
