  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q158",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q158",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You have a Fabric warehouse that contains two tables named DimDate and Trips.\nDimDate contains the following fields.\nTrips contains the following fields.\nYou need to compare the average miles per trip for statutory holidays versus non-statutory holidays.\nHow should you complete the T-SQL statement? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "0",
        "label": "Select d.IsHoliday,  ______  as MilesPerTrip",
        "options": [
          "(count(t.tripID) / sum(t.tripDistance))",
          "(sum(t.tripDistance)/count(t.tripID))",
          "Sum(t.tripDistance)/t.tripID)"
        ],
        "answer": "(sum(t.tripDistance)/count(t.tripID))"
      },
      {
        "id": "1",
        "label": "______  d.IsHoliday",
        "options": [
          "group by",
          "order by",
          "where"
        ],
        "answer": "group by"
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>**`(sum(t.tripDistance)/count(t.tripID))` — `group by`.**\n\n```sql\nSELECT d.IsHoliday, (SUM(t.tripDistance) / COUNT(t.tripID)) AS MilesPerTrip\nFROM dbo.Trips t\nINNER JOIN dbo.DimDate d ON t.dateID = d.DateID\nGROUP BY d.IsHoliday;\n```\n\n**Blank 1 — miles *per trip*** is total distance divided by number of trips: `SUM(tripDistance) / COUNT(tripID)`. Get the order right.\n- `(count(t.tripID) / sum(t.tripDistance))` is upside down — trips per mile.\n- `Sum(t.tripDistance)/t.tripID)` divides an aggregate by a raw column that is neither aggregated nor grouped, which T-SQL rejects.\n\n**Blank 2 — `group by`.** The comparison is *&quot;statutory holidays **versus** non-statutory holidays&quot;*, i.e. one row per value of `IsHoliday`. `GROUP BY d.IsHoliday` produces exactly two rows, and it is also required syntactically because `d.IsHoliday` appears unaggregated in the `SELECT` list alongside aggregates.\n- `order by` only sorts; the query would still fail to compile.\n- `where` filters rows before aggregation and cannot produce a per-group result.</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "SELECT — GROUP BY (Transact-SQL)",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/sql/t-sql/queries/select-group-by-transact-sql?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [
      "Original question exhibit files not supplied: p372_i1.png, p372_i2.png, p372_i3.png"
    ],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "json:T1Q158"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "missingExhibits": [
