  {
    "id": "new-json-t1q186",
    "sourceId": "json:T1Q186",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<pre>You have a Fabric eventhouse named Eventhouse1 that contains a table named Weatherdata. A sample of the data in Weatherdata is shown in the\nfollowing table.\nYou plan to use a KQL queryset to manipulate the data in Eventhouse1. The result set must have the following columns.\nYou need to build the query.\nWhich four KQL statements should you use in sequence? To answer, move the appropriate statements from the list of statements to the answer\narea and arrange them in the correct order.</pre>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "0",
        "label": "Step 1",
        "options": [
          "Weatherdata",
          "| sort by Datetime asc",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature)",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature,2)",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - next(Temperature,1)",
          "| summarize Delta_temperature = sum(Temperature) - sum(prev(Temperature)) by Datetime",
          "| project Datetime, Lat, Long, Temperature, Delta_temperature"
        ],
        "answer": "Weatherdata"
      },
      {
        "id": "1",
        "label": "Step 2",
        "options": [
          "Weatherdata",
          "| sort by Datetime asc",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature)",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature,2)",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - next(Temperature,1)",
          "| summarize Delta_temperature = sum(Temperature) - sum(prev(Temperature)) by Datetime",
          "| project Datetime, Lat, Long, Temperature, Delta_temperature"
        ],
        "answer": "| sort by Datetime asc"
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "label": "Step 3",
        "options": [
          "Weatherdata",
          "| sort by Datetime asc",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature)",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature,2)",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - next(Temperature,1)",
          "| summarize Delta_temperature = sum(Temperature) - sum(prev(Temperature)) by Datetime",
          "| project Datetime, Lat, Long, Temperature, Delta_temperature"
        ],
        "answer": "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature)"
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "label": "Step 4",
        "options": [
          "Weatherdata",
          "| sort by Datetime asc",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature)",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature,2)",
          "| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - next(Temperature,1)",
          "| summarize Delta_temperature = sum(Temperature) - sum(prev(Temperature)) by Datetime",
          "| project Datetime, Lat, Long, Temperature, Delta_temperature"
        ],
        "answer": "| project Datetime, Lat, Long, Temperature, Delta_temperature"
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<pre>**Weatherdata → `| sort by Datetime asc` → `| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature)` → `| project Datetime, Lat, Long, Temperature, Delta_temperature`.**\n\n&gt; 📄 **Note on the exhibit.** The statements list captured in the PDF shows only six tiles and is **missing the `| project …` tile**, even though the question asks for *four* statements and the required output has a fixed column list. A commenter hits the same problem (*&quot;my screenshot is not even showing the project&quot;*). The tile is restored above. The PDF&#x27;s &quot;suggested answer&quot; panel is likewise garbled — it lists `summarize` in the answer area, which cannot be right (see below).\n\n### Step 1 — `Weatherdata`\n\nEvery KQL query starts with the tabular source. Nothing else can come first.\n\n### Step 2 — `| sort by Datetime asc` **before** the extend\n\nThis is the step people drop, and it is the one being tested. `prev()` returns *&quot;a value of a column from a row at some offset prior to the current row&quot;* **in serialized order** — it has no notion of &quot;the previous timestamp&quot;, only &quot;the previous row as currently arranged&quot;. Rows come back from an eventhouse in no guaranteed order, so without an explicit `sort by Datetime asc` the deltas would be computed against arbitrary neighbours. Sort first, then `prev()` means what you want it to mean.\n\n### Step 3 — `| extend Delta_temperature = Temperature - prev(Temperature)`\n\nThe required column is *&quot;Difference in temperature from the preceding row and the current row&quot;*. Check each candidate tile against that:\n\n| Tile | What it computes | |\n|---|---|:-:|\n| **`Temperature - prev(Temperature)`** | current − **immediately preceding** row | **✔** |\n| `Temperature - prev(Temperature,2)` | current − the row **two** back (offset 2) | ✘ wrong offset |\n| `Temperature - next(Temperature,1)` | current − the **following** row — sign flipped and looking the wrong way | ✘ |\n| `summarize Delta_temperature = sum(Temperature) - sum(prev(Temperature)) by Datetime` | **collapses rows**, destroying Lat/Long/Temperature, and `prev()` is not even legal inside `summarize` | ✘ |\n\nThe default offset of `prev(column)` is **1**, which is exactly &quot;the preceding row&quot; — writing `prev(Temperature, 1)` would be identical.\n\n### Step 4 — `| project Datetime, Lat, Long, Temperature, Delta_temperature`\n\nThe required result set is an exact five-column list. `extend` has **added** `Delta_temperature` while keeping `Pressure` and `Wind`, so a `project` is needed to trim the output down to — and order — the requested columns.\n\n**The shape to memorise for &quot;difference from previous row&quot; in KQL: `Source | sort by &lt;time&gt; asc | extend delta = x - prev(x) | project …`.**\n\n*(Same operator pair as T1Q178 — `extend` adds, `project` selects.)*</pre>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [
      {
        "title": "prev() (KQL)",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/kusto/query/prev-function?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      },
      {
        "title": "sort operator (KQL)",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/kusto/query/sort-operator?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      },
      {
        "title": "extend operator (KQL)",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/kusto/query/extend-operator?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      },
      {
        "title": "project operator (KQL)",
        "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/kusto/query/project-operator?wt.mc_id=studentamb_657938"
      }
    ],
    "blockers": [
      "Original question exhibit files not supplied: p424_i1.png, p424_i2.png"
    ],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "json:T1Q186"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "missingExhibits": [
      "p424_i1.png",
      "p424_i2.png"
    ],
    "missingAnswerImages": [
      "p424_i3.png",
      "p424_i4.png"
    ]
