  {
    "id": "new-hub-dumps-1-r1",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:dumps:1",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>Which syntax should you use in a notebook to access the Research division data for Productline1?</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "spark.read.format(“delta”).load(“Tables/ResearchProduct”)"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "spark.read.format(“delta”).load(“Files/ResearchProduct”)"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "external_table(‘Tables/ResearchProduct)"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "external_table(ResearchProduct)"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "A"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>The shortcut ResearchProduct sits in the Tables section of the lakehouse as a Delta table. Reading it with spark.read.format(&quot;delta&quot;).load(&quot;Tables/ResearchProduct&quot;) addresses that table directly. The Files section holds raw files rather than the shortcut table, and external_table is KQL syntax, not Spark.</p>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "study-hub:dumps:1:row1"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
    "caseLabel": "Contoso"
  },
  {
    "id": "new-hub-dumps-2-r2",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:dumps:2",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You have a Fabric tenant named Tenant1 that contains a workspace named WS1. WS1 uses a capacity named C1 and contains a dataset named DS1. You need to ensure read-write access to DS1 is available by using XMLA endpoint. What should be modified first?</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "the DS1 settings"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "the WS1 settings"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "the C1 settings"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "the Tenant1 settings"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "C"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>C. the C1 settings.</p>\n<p>To enable read-write access via the XMLA endpoint, the XMLA endpoint must be set to Read/Write at the capacity level.</p>\n<p>In Power BI / Fabric:</p>\n<p>XMLA endpoint configuration is controlled at the Premium capacity level</p>\n<p>Workspaces inherit this setting from the capacity.</p>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "study-hub:dumps:2:row2"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
