  {
    "id": "new-hub-dumps-44-r44",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:dumps:44",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Workspace1. Workspace1 contains a warehouse named DW1. DW1 contains two tables named Employees and Sales. All users have read access to Dw1. You need to implement access controls to meet the following requirements: - For the Sales table, ensure that the users can see only the sales data from their respective region. - For the Employees table, restrict access to all Personally Identifiable Information (PII). - Maintain access to unrestricted data for all the users. What should you use for each table? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area. NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>\n<p>Answer Area</p><ul><li>Employees: Column-level security / Item permissions / Row-level security (RLS) / Workspace permissions</li><li>Sales: Column-level security / Item permissions / Row-level security (RLS) / Workspace permissions</li></ul>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "d1",
        "label": "Employees:",
        "options": [
          "Column-level security",
          "Item permissions",
          "Row-level security (RLS)",
          "Workspace permissions"
        ],
        "answer": "Column-level security"
      },
      {
        "id": "d2",
        "label": "Sales:",
        "options": [
          "Column-level security",
          "Item permissions",
          "Row-level security (RLS)",
          "Workspace permissions"
        ],
        "answer": "Row-level security (RLS)"
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>Restricting PII columns is column-level security, applied to the Employees table. Limiting rows by region is row-level security, applied to the Sales table.</p>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "study-hub:dumps:44:row44"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
