    "caseLabel": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "new-hub-dumps-45-r45",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:dumps:45",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>Your company has a finance department. You have a Fabric tenant, an Azure Storage account named storage1, and a Microsoft Entra group named Group1. Group1 contains the users in the finance department. You need to create a new workspace named Workspace1 in the tenant. The solution must meet the following requirements: - Ensure that the finance department users can create and edit items in Workspace1. - Ensure that Workspace1 can securely access storage1 to read and write data. - Ensure that you are the only admin of Workspace1. - Minimize administrative effort. You create Workspace1. Which two actions should you perform next? Each correct answer presents part of the solution. NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "Assign the Contributor role to Group1."
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "Create a workspace identity."
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "Assign the Admin role to yourself."
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "Assign the Contributor role to each finance department user."
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "multi",
    "answers": [
      "A",
      "B"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>Assigning the Contributor role to Group1 gives every finance user create and edit rights in one step, which minimizes administrative effort. A workspace identity lets the workspace itself securely access storage1 to read and write data. You are already the workspace admin as its creator, and assigning the role to each user individually would be extra effort.</p>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "study-hub:dumps:45:row45"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
    "caseLabel": "Contoso"
  },
  {
    "id": "new-hub-dumps-46-r46",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:dumps:46",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You have a Fabric tenant. You need to configure OneLake security for users shown in the following table. The solution must follow the principle of least privilege. Which permission should you assign to each user? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area. NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>\n<p>Answer Area</p><ul><li>User1: Read / ReadAll / ReadData</li><li>User2: Read / ReadAll / ReadData</li></ul>",
    "contextHtml": "<div><div>Exhibit (transcribed): Required access</div><div><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Required access</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>User1</td><td>Read all the Spark data.</td></tr><tr><td>User2</td><td>Read all the SQL endpoint data.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "d1",
        "label": "User1:",
        "options": [
          "Read",
          "ReadAll",
          "ReadData"
        ],
        "answer": "ReadAll"
      },
      {
        "id": "d2",
        "label": "User2:",
        "options": [
          "Read",
          "ReadAll",
          "ReadData"
        ],
        "answer": "ReadData"
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>Reading data through Spark and the OneLake APIs needs the ReadAll permission, so User1 gets ReadAll. Reading data through the SQL endpoint needs the ReadData permission, so User2 gets ReadData.</p>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "study-hub:dumps:46:row46"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
    "caseLabel": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "new-hub-dumps-47-r47",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:dumps:47",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You have a Fabric tenant that contains a workspace named Enterprise. Enterprise contains a semantic model named Model1. Model1 contains a date parameter named Date1 that was created in Power Query. You build a deployment pipeline named Enterprise Data that includes two stages named Development and Test. You assign the Enterprise workspace to the Development stage. You need to perform the following actions: - Create a workspace named Enterprise [Test] and assign the workspace to the Test stage. - Configure a rule that will modify the value of Date1 when changes are deployed to the Test stage. Which two settings should you use? To answer, select the appropriate settings in the answer area. NOTE: Each correct answer is worth one point.</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "z1",
        "text": "Test stage settings"
      },
      {
        "id": "z2",
        "text": "Deploy to this stage or Assign a workspace"
      },
      {
        "id": "z3",
        "text": "Deployment history"
      },
      {
        "id": "z4",
        "text": "Manage Access"
      },
      {
        "id": "z5",
        "text": "Settings"
      },
      {
        "id": "z6",
        "text": "Development stage"
      },
      {
        "id": "z7",
        "text": "Enterprise workspace"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "multi",
    "answers": [
      "z1",
      "z2"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>The Test stage has no workspace yet, so you assign one using the &quot;Deploy to this stage or Assign a workspace&quot; area. Deployment rules such as changing the Date1 parameter are configured in the Test stage settings, using the pencil icon on the Test stage.</p>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
