    "caseLabel": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "new-hub-dumps-54-r54",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:dumps:54",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You need to resolve the issue with the pricing group classification. How should you complete the T-SQL statement? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area. NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>\n<p>Answer Area</p><pre><code>CREATE [dropdown 1] [dbo].[ProductsWithPricingGroup]\nAS\nSELECT ProductId,\n    ProductName,\n    ProductCategory,\n    ListPrice,\n    [dropdown 2]\n        WHEN ListPrice &lt;= 50 THEN &#x27;low&#x27;\n        [dropdown 3]\n        WHEN ListPrice &gt; 1000 THEN &#x27;high&#x27;\n    END AS PricingGroup\nFROM dbo.Products</code></pre><ul><li>Dropdown 1: FUNCTION / PROCEDURE / TABLE / VIEW</li><li>Dropdown 2: CASE / COALESCE / IIF / SET</li><li>Dropdown 3: WHEN (ListPrice &gt; 50 AND ListPrice &lt;= 1000 ) THEN &#x27;medium&#x27; / WHEN (ListPrice &gt;= 50 AND ListPrice &lt; 1000 ) THEN &#x27;medium&#x27; / WHEN (ListPrice BETWEEN 50 AND 1000 ) THEN &#x27;medium&#x27;</li></ul>",
    "contextHtml": "<pre>CREATE [dropdown 1] [dbo].[ProductsWithPricingGroup]\nAS\nSELECT ProductId,\n    ProductName,\n    ProductCategory,\n    ListPrice,\n    [dropdown 2]\n        WHEN ListPrice &lt;= 50 THEN &#x27;low&#x27;\n        [dropdown 3]\n        WHEN ListPrice &gt; 1000 THEN &#x27;high&#x27;\n    END AS PricingGroup\nFROM dbo.Products</pre>",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "d1",
        "label": "d1",
        "options": [
          "FUNCTION",
          "PROCEDURE",
          "TABLE",
          "VIEW"
        ],
        "answer": "VIEW"
      },
      {
        "id": "d2",
        "label": "d2",
        "options": [
          "CASE",
          "COALESCE",
          "IIF",
          "SET"
        ],
        "answer": "CASE"
      },
      {
        "id": "d3",
        "label": "d3",
        "options": [
          "WHEN (ListPrice > 50 AND ListPrice <= 1000 ) THEN 'medium'",
          "WHEN (ListPrice >= 50 AND ListPrice < 1000 ) THEN 'medium'",
          "WHEN (ListPrice BETWEEN 50 AND 1000 ) THEN 'medium'"
        ],
        "answer": "WHEN (ListPrice BETWEEN 50 AND 1000 ) THEN 'medium'"
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>VIEW: from an existing table.</p>\n<p>* CASE: correct syntax before the WHENs.</p>\n<p>* WHEN ListPrice BETWEEN 50 AND 1000 THEN &#x27;medium&#x27;: the other two options miss value 1000; on the other hand, the BETWEEN includes both 50 and 1000.</p>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "study-hub:dumps:54:row54"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
    "caseLabel": "Litware"
  },
  {
    "id": "new-hub-dumps-55-r55",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:dumps:55",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You are building a solution by using a Fabric notebook. You have a Spark DataFrame assigned to a variable named df. The DataFrame returns four columns. You need to change the data type of a string column named Age to integer. The solution must return a DataFrame that includes all the columns. How should you complete the code? To answer, drag the appropriate values to the correct targets. Each value may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content. NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>\n<p>Answer Area</p><p>Values: cast / col / get / select / selectExpr / transform / withColumn</p><pre><code>df. [drop target 1] (&quot;age&quot;, [drop target 2] (&quot;age&quot;). [drop target 3] (&quot;int&quot;)).show()</code></pre>",
    "contextHtml": "<pre>df. [drop target 1] (&quot;age&quot;, [drop target 2] (&quot;age&quot;). [drop target 3] (&quot;int&quot;)).show()</pre>",
    "options": [],
    "controls": [
      {
        "id": "t1",
        "label": "Target 1",
        "options": [
          "cast",
          "col",
          "get",
          "select",
          "selectExpr",
          "transform",
          "withColumn"
        ],
        "answer": "withColumn"
      },
      {
        "id": "t2",
        "label": "Target 2",
        "options": [
          "cast",
          "col",
          "get",
          "select",
          "selectExpr",
          "transform",
          "withColumn"
        ],
        "answer": "col"
      },
      {
        "id": "t3",
        "label": "Target 3",
        "options": [
          "cast",
          "col",
          "get",
          "select",
          "selectExpr",
          "transform",
          "withColumn"
        ],
        "answer": "cast"
      }
    ],
    "mode": "controls",
    "answers": [],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>withColumn adds or replaces the age column, col references the age column, and cast converts it to int: df.withColumn(&quot;age&quot;, col(&quot;age&quot;).cast(&quot;int&quot;)).</p>",
    "images": [],
