  {
    "id": "new-hub-dumps-57-r57",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:dumps:57",
    "exam": "DP-600",
    "stemHtml": "<p>Which syntax should you use in a notebook to access the Research division data for Productline1?</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "spark.sql(\"SELECT * FROM Lakehouse1.Tables.ResearchProduct\")"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "spark.read.format(\"delta\").load(\"Tables/productline1/ResearchProduct\")"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "external_table(ResearchProduct)"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "spark.read.format(\"delta\").load(\"Tables/ResearchProduct\")"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>The shortcut ResearchProduct sits in the Tables section of the lakehouse as a Delta table, so it is read with spark.read.format(&quot;delta&quot;).load(&quot;Tables/ResearchProduct&quot;). &quot;Tables&quot; is not a schema in Spark SQL three-part naming, so the Spark SQL option is wrong, and the productline1 path does not exist.</p>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "study-hub:dumps:57:row57"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
