  {
    "id": "new-hub-pl300-32-r32",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:pl300:32",
    "exam": "PL-300",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You have a PBIX file that imports data from a Microsoft Excel data source stored in a file share on a local network. You are notified that the Excel data source was moved to a new location. You need to update the PBIX file to use the new location. What are three ways to achieve the goal? Each correct answer presents a complete solution. NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "From the Datasets settings of the Power BI service, configure the data source credentials."
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "From the Data source settings in Power BI Desktop, configure the file path."
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "From Current File in Power BI Desktop, configure the Data Load settings."
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "From Power Query Editor, use the formula bar to configure the file path for the applied step."
      },
      {
        "id": "E",
        "text": "From Advanced Editor in Power Query Editor, configure the file path in the M code."
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "multi",
    "answers": [
      "B",
      "D",
      "E"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>B.From the Data source settings in Power BI Desktop, configure the file path.</p>\n<p>D.From Power Query Editor, use the formula bar to configure the file path for the applied step.</p>\n<p>E.From Advanced Editor in Power Query Editor, configure the file path in the M code.</p>\n<p>Why the Other Options Are Incorrect:</p>\n<p>A. From the Datasets settings of the Power BI service, configure the data source credentials.</p>\n<p>This option is related to managing authentication and credentials to access the data source (e.g., user permissions or authentication methods), but it does not handle the file path or location change.</p>\n<p>It’s useful for cloud-based sources, but for local network data sources, the file path needs to be updated within Power BI Desktop or the Power Query Editor.</p>\n<p>C. From Current File in Power BI Desktop, configure the Data Load settings.</p>\n<p>The Current File option in Power BI Desktop allows you to change data load settings, but it does not address the file path for an Excel data source. This setting is more related to options like whether to import or load data from the current file into the model, rather than specifying the path of the Excel file.</p>\n<p>Summary:</p>\n<p>To update the file path for the Excel data source after it has been moved:</p>\n<p>B, D, and E are the appropriate solutions, as they allow you to configure the new file path within the data source settings, Power Query Editor, or M code.</p>",
    "images": [],
    "refs": [],
    "blockers": [],
    "sourceRecords": [
      "study-hub:pl300:32:row32"
    ],
    "review": "Source-supplied answer; not independently validated",
    "revealImages": [],
    "caseLabel": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "new-hub-pl300-33-r33",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:pl300:33",
    "exam": "PL-300",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You have a Power BI semantic model that contains the data sources shown in the following table.</p>\n<p>You need to configure the privacy level s of the data sources. What should you configure for each data source? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area. NOTE: Each correct answer is worth one point.</p>\n<p>Answer Area</p>\n<ul><li>Employee review data: None / Organizational / Private / Public</li><li>Sales opportunities: None / Organizational / Private / Public</li></ul>",
    "contextHtml": "<div><div>Exhibit (transcribed): Data sources</div><div><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Employee review data</td><td>Contains sensitive information. Must &lt;b&gt;NOT&lt;/b&gt; be folded into any other data sources</td></tr><tr><td>Sales opportunities</td><td>Contains less sensitive information. Must only be available internally</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>",
