  {
    "id": "new-hub-pl300-34-r34",
    "sourceId": "study-hub:pl300:34",
    "exam": "PL-300",
    "stemHtml": "<p>You plan to use Power BI Desktop to create a bug tracking dashboard that will pull data from Analytics in Azure DevOps. From Power BI Desktop, you need to configure a data connector to authenticate to Azure DevOps. The solution must meet the following requirements: •Use Analytics views. •Filter data from the cloud. Which connector should you use?</p>",
    "contextHtml": "",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "A",
        "text": "OData queries"
      },
      {
        "id": "B",
        "text": "Azure DevOps (Boards only)"
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "Azure DevOps Server (Boards only)"
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "OData Feed"
      }
    ],
    "controls": [],
    "mode": "single",
    "answers": [
      "D"
    ],
    "explanationHtml": "<p>D. OData Feed.</p>\n<p>Azure DevOps Analytics views are exposed through an OData endpoint.</p>\n<p>The OData Feed connector in Power BI Desktop:</p>\n<p>Authenticates to Azure DevOps Analytics</p>\n<p>Supports server-side filtering, meaning data is filtered in the cloud before import</p>\n<p>Is the recommended approach for Analytics views</p>\n<p>Why not the others?</p>",
